<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Amorgos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/322-bce">322 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war">Lamian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amorgos">Amorgos</a> was a naval battle fought in 322 BCE near the island of Amorgos during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war">Lamian War</a>. The Macedonian fleet under Cleitus the White defeated the Athenian navy, which had joined the Greek rising against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antipater">Antipater</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>. The defeat ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>' career as a great naval power and was followed by a Macedonian garrison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piraeus">Piraeus</a> and a restricted franchise.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-amorgos.jpg" alt="Battle of Amorgos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliwan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amorgos-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
